item+ function src/plan.rs :: compute :: pub fn compute(tasks: &[TaskInput], current: &DiskObs, history: &[DiskObs], host: (f64, f64), gate: &GateInputs) -> PlanData { :: Compute the plan: - byte gate: the worse of the lenses that are ON (see evaluate_gate) — the volume lens judges the measured volume's free fraction; the quota lens, only where a node configures it, reproduces the old absolute ceiling (AMBER 95 GB / RED 102 GB, thresholds anchored to the 2026-11-08 EDQUOT failure at ~106 GB on the Muse VM's staging quota — a real ceiling on that one machine, a false verdict everywhere else). - file gate (v2.2): AMBER/RED at the configured counts under the named staging root — the count is the faster-moving half of the disk currency, and a byte-only gate can sit GREEN while the count runs at the wall. - disk gate = the worse of the two halves. - forecast gate (v2.3, re-based on the lenses in v1.0.3): a GREEN disk gate escalates to AMBER when the nearest crossing projected under the node's configured lenses is within 3 days. A planner that only watches crossings gives no lead time — and a forecast that projects levels the gate no longer reads gives false alarms instead. :: doc comment :: 592 :: 1
