item+ function src/plan.rs :: forecast_gate :: pub fn forecast_gate(history: &[DiskObs], cfg: &GateConfig, total_bytes: Option<u64>) -> Forecast { :: The forecast computation (v2.3 semantics, re-based on the gate's lenses in v1.0.3): rate growth from the history's last two observations, then project days to the crossings of the SAME thresholds evaluate_gate reads — the volume lens's free fractions of this volume's total, the quota lens's ceilings (only when the node has that lens on), and the file lens's configured counts. Until v1.0.3 the byte half projected the legacy absolute levels (95/102 GB) whatever the node's configuration, so the forecast contradicted the gate it forecasts on every ranch volume.  A crossing the current reading has already reached is the gate's verdict, not a forecast: projecting it would report 0.0 days for a level the lenses already own — exactly the v1.0.2 fleet failure, where the second plan on a healthy ranch node flipped to FORECAST AMBER because its volume had long since passed a ceiling that no longer applies to it. Flat or falling growth projects nothing, and nothing is projected beyond FORECAST_HORIZON_DAYS. Fewer than two usable observations degrades to unavailable — never invented. :: doc comment :: 447 :: 1
