item+ const src/plan.rs :: FORECAST_HORIZON_DAYS :: pub const FORECAST_HORIZON_DAYS: f64 = 365.0; :: How far ahead a crossing projection is reported, in days. A linear rate read off the last interval is a short-horizon instrument: a crossing farther out than this will be re-projected hundreds of times before it can matter, and naming a day count for it lends it a precision it does not have. Crossings beyond the horizon are reported as no crossing. :: doc comment :: 457 :: 1
item+ const src/plan.rs :: FORECAST_WINDOW_INTERVALS :: pub const FORECAST_WINDOW_INTERVALS: usize = 7; :: How many of the most recent intervals the forecast rates (v1.2.1). The window bounds the median's memory: older intervals fall out instead of anchoring the rate forever, and a history shorter than the window simply contributes every interval it has. :: doc comment :: 464 :: 1
item+ const src/plan.rs :: PLAN_VERSION :: pub const PLAN_VERSION: &str = concat!("v", env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")); :: A fixed value named PLAN_VERSION, set to concat!("v", env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")). :: signature :: 59 :: 0
item+ const src/plan.rs :: VERSION :: pub const VERSION: &str = env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION"); :: The build's own version, from the Cargo manifest — the single source every user-facing version stamp derives from (v1.7.2). Hand-written version literals drifted three releases behind (the "qexo v1.4.0" help/status prints on a v1.7.1 binary); deriving them makes that drift impossible by construction. :: doc comment :: 58 :: 1
