item+ function src/wire.rs :: accept_wire_bundle :: pub fn accept_wire_bundle(lat: &mut Lattice, gpg: &Gpg, bytes: &[u8]) -> AcceptOutcome { :: Accept a wire bundle on this node (§3.4), in the acceptance rule's order: parse → the signer is a registered peer and the signature verifies → the per-universe hashes match → capability fit → dedup and fencing (§4.3, §4.6 combination 2). On acceptance the attempt is filed and the assignment record written — LIVE (no `status:` line). A replay of the same (item, sha256, attempt) returns the original acceptance receipt and writes nothing. A lower attempt, or an equal attempt carrying a different hash, is refused as stale (the fencing rule); a higher attempt supersedes live older assignments, which are retired in the same pass. Refusals file a refusal receipt in this node's ledgers (§4.6 combination 5's shape) and never file an attempt. Mutates in memory; the caller saves. :: doc comment :: 896 :: 1
