item+ function src/wire.rs :: draw :: pub fn draw(eligible: &[String], seed: u64) -> Option<String> { :: The draw: splitmix64 over the round's seed, modulo the eligible set — uniform over the set as listed, and the eligible set is always listed in a stable order (self first, then peers by cluster), so a round replays exactly from its receipted seed (§6). :: doc comment :: 1097 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: eligibility :: pub fn eligibility(f: &NodeFacts, required_caps: &[String], bundle_bytes: u64) -> Result<(), String> { :: The eligibility verdict (§6, in the spec's own order): (a) reachability, (b) load and temperature, (c) a resident agent at work, (d) data locality — then capability fit. `Ok(())` is eligible; the `Err` is the exclusion's reason, tagged with its criterion, which the placement receipt carries verbatim (§14: exclusions are recorded, never silent). :: doc comment :: 1050 :: 1
