item+ function src/wire.rs :: file_attempt :: pub fn file_attempt(lat: &mut Lattice, pb: &ParsedBundle, assignment_book: u32) -> Result<(), String> { :: File an accepted bundle's attempt (§3.3, §3.4): the attempt universe (attempt N → universe N+1) holds the executor's working copy of the item — the record copy with `home:` set to the origin node, `bundle-sha256:` set, state dispatched — the brief, and the bundle's paperwork under the assignment's Book family. Universe 1 holds a second copy at the item's home address — the record the oracle and the local verbs read; the attempt itself (its heartbeat lines, its checkpoint scrolls) lives in the stratum, never merged into universe 1 (§3.3). An address already holding a DIFFERENT bundle's copy is a named refusal — two bundles never share a home address in a stratum. :: doc comment :: 681 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: file_origin_snapshot :: pub fn file_origin_snapshot(lat: &mut Lattice, pb: &ParsedBundle, assignment_book: u32) { :: File the ORIGIN's as-dispatched snapshot of an attempt (§4.6 combination 7's conservative reading: attempts homed here need chain universes ≥ attempts+1 in the origin's own state). The snapshot is the bundle's contents verbatim — the pristine record copy, the brief, the manifest, the context provenances — never the executor's working copy; the doctor's combination 6 recomputes from either form (the recomputation strips exactly the fields acceptance adds). :: doc comment :: 737 :: 1
