item+ function src/wire.rs :: place :: pub fn place(facts: &[NodeFacts], required_caps: &[String], bundle_bytes: u64, to: Option<&str>) -> Placement { :: Run one placement round over gathered facts. With `--to`, the named node is the target — but its eligibility is still computed and recorded, and an ineligible named node places nothing (§6: naming overrides the draw, never the gates). :: doc comment :: 1313 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: recompute_bundle_sha256 :: pub fn recompute_bundle_sha256(lat: &Lattice, item_addr: &Coord, attempt: u32) -> Option<String> { :: Recompute an accepted attempt's bundle hash from its stratum: the manifest verbatim (filed under the assignment's Book family), the pristine record copy reconstructed from the working copy (the acceptance's own writes stripped, the pre-transition state restored), the brief, and the context universes regrouped by their provenance scrolls. Returns None when the stratum lacks the pieces (combination 7 owns that finding) and Some(hash) otherwise. The origin's as-dispatched snapshot recomputes identically — its record copy is already pristine, so the strips are no-ops. :: doc comment :: 2830 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: sign_bundle :: pub fn sign_bundle(gpg: &Gpg, bundle: &Bundle) -> Result<String, String> { :: Sign a built bundle into its wire bytes: the detached signature over the manifest's exact bytes at the anchor's Scroll 2 (§3.4 — the releases cluster's manifest+signature pattern). :: doc comment :: 464 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: unsigned_chain_bytes :: pub fn unsigned_chain_bytes(universes: &[Phext]) -> String { :: The canonical bytes a bundle's hash is taken over: the chain of its universes with the signature scroll removed. Deterministic in the item record, the brief, the context selections, the origin identity, the attempt, and the routed bridge (§9.2 — the choice is cited in the manifest, so a different route is a different bundle) — nothing else (§4.3). :: doc comment :: 241 :: 1
item+ function src/wire.rs :: verify_bundle :: pub fn verify_bundle(lat: &Lattice, gpg: &Gpg, pb: &ParsedBundle) -> Result<(), String> { :: Verify a parsed bundle (§3.4, in the acceptance rule's order): the claimed signer must be a registered peer in this node's state and the detached signature must verify under that identity (registering a peer imported its key — verification is the shipped path); every context universe's hash must match the manifest's list. The bundle hash is carried by the identity rule (§4.3), not verified against the manifest — the manifest cannot contain it; it is checked against the item's record by the callers that hold one. :: doc comment :: 583 :: 1
